WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.550
Take one cell from your
skin and one from a nerve.

2
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.890
Read the DNA inside each.

3
00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:08.280
Gene for gene, it's the same.

4
00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:11.980
Almost every cell in a body
carries the same genome.

5
00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:15.820
Yet the two cells look nothing
alike, and do different jobs.

6
00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:20.730
So if the instructions are identical,
why doesn't a skin cell act like a nerve

7
00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:21.740
cell?

8
00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:24.810
In this mission, you'll
follow a gene from DNA,

9
00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:28.560
to messenger RNA, to a
protein that does its job.

10
00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:33.220
Then you'll find the step in that chain
that acts as the main control point.

11
00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:37.710
Your mission: explain why a skin
cell doesn't act like a nerve cell,

12
00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:39.890
when both carry the same genes.
